  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the current best at 0.542 acc, clearly outperforming config_002 (resnet50) and confirming that multimodal + multiprofile + scgpt + imagenet_vit_l is the strongest backbone. The key untested dimension on this backbone is aggregation strategy. Question: Will transformer aggregation (config_015) outperform avgpool by capturing richer inter-profile relationships while retaining the proven scgpt/imagenet_vit_l/weighted-fusion components? Rationale: This is a minimal, high-information extension of the best config—only one variable (aggregation) changes, so any accuracy delta is cleanly attributable. Transformer aggregation is the most architecturally impactful remaining choice for multiprofile settings and could yield a meaningful jump over simple averaging. Expected cost: ~3.5–4.5 GPU hrs (moderately higher than config_018's 2.94 due to transformer attention over profiles, but well within budget with 6 experiments remaining and only 7.48 GPU hrs used so far)."
